title: The least machine is 4 vCPU, 8 GB and at least 40 GB of disk (80 comfortable); below 8 GB, a build beside the servers is what gives first.
pid: 80c71bef-0d79-4042-8a7d-cb38a4f1852f
body: |2-
  At a moment of building, memory holds: your server over your notes
  1.3 GB, Top's server 1.3 GB, one or two specialists' servers 0.4 GB
  each, one or two Claude programs 0.4 GB each, the build 3.7 GB
  (2.2 GB if it builds two at once instead of four), and the system with
  an editor about 1 GB. That is about 8 to 9 GB, or 7 with the smaller
  build. So 8 GB works with builds kept to two at once; 16 GB works
  without care. Below 8 GB the build would push into swap, and a
  35-second rebuild would become minutes (estimated).
  Cores give way more gently: on two cores a rebuild after an edit took
  45 s instead of 35, and a build from nothing would take about twice as
  long (estimated).
  Disk: about 22 GB is in use, of which the build folder is 9 GB and
  grows until cleaned; 40 GB is the floor, 80 GB comfortable.
  If your own server stays on this laptop, take 1.3 GB off.
contains:
